From 4428ca5d6b46b93709c39f416fb607b1cfa8ccc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: japq7s <japiotr123@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:18:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/33] pipeline: camss: Add an IFE inline pixel pipe ISP

The VFE line that receives a sensor on SM8450 and newer has a pixel pipe
that processes the frame on its way to memory: demux and black level,
WB gains, demosaic, colour correction, gamma and colour space transform,
with the parameters taken from a v4l2-isp parameters buffer per frame.

Add a CamssIsp implementation for it. The CSI decoder is linked to the
pixel line of the VFE whose RDI0 the CSI side picked, and NV12 is
captured from the line straight into the request buffers: there is no
raw buffer, so the CSI side does not stream and raw streams are refused.

The soft IPA computes the parameters, which are translated to the WB,
colour correction and gamma blocks as for the OPE. Its statistics are
computed on the CPU from a sparse sampling of each NV12 frame, with the
gamma curve, the colour correction and the gains that produced the frame
undone so that the IPA sees the sensor values it expects. On a static
scene the inverted means match the raw frame within 1%.

LIBCAMERA_CAMSS_IFE=0 falls back to the OPE or the software ISP.

This backport to v0.7.2 also carries the finer grained locking of the
camss pipeline handler ("camss: Use finer grained locking /
disableLinks()") without the OPE, which SM8450 does not have, and uses
the v0.7.2 soft IPA: its setIspParams() event carries no frame number,
so the frames waiting for parameters are kept in order. Lens controls
from the IPA move the focus lens, and the statistics carry the focus
measure of the contrast autofocus, computed on the luma of the centre
third of the frame.

Signed-off-by: japq7s <japiotr123@proton.me>
